  baseData:
    id: CH-1500AD-02
    itemName: Jar With Dragon
    itemDescription: White porcelain painted with cobalt blue, a style that first
      flourished in China in the fourteenth century, is arguably the most important
      development in the history of ceramics. Commissioned by the court, this spectacular
      storage jar, made in the kilns in Jingdezhen, is dated to the rule of the Xuande
      emperor by an inscription on its shoulder. Its painted decoration features
      an animated dragon undulating across a sparsely clouded sky.
